# Feature module structure

Each domain lives under `src/features/<domain>/`. Reference: `src/features/quotes/`.

## Layout

```text
features/<domain>/
├── pages/<pageGroup>/     # Page + colocated *.test.tsx
├── components/<group>/    # UI grouped by concern (camelCase folder names)
├── hooks/                 # Domain-specific hooks (mutations, workflows)
└── lib/                   # Pure domain logic (filters, row builders, constants)
```

## Components

- Group related UI in `components/<group>/` (e.g. `quoteHeaderForm/`, `quotesFilters/`, `quoteLinesTable/`).
- One main export per file; file name matches the export (`QuoteCard.tsx` → `QuoteCard`).
- **No barrel files** in `components/` root unless a group has many public exports.
- Import directly: `@/features/quotes/components/quoteCard/QuoteCard`
- Shared props types: export from the primary component in the group; siblings import with `import type`.

## Pages

- Prefer `pages/<pageGroup>/<PageName>.tsx` with test beside it (`QuotesPage.test.tsx`).
- Pages compose feature components; keep data-fetching and routing here, not in leaf components when possible.

## Hooks vs lib

| Put in | Examples |
|--------|----------|
| `hooks/` | RTK mutation wrappers, snackbar + save flows (`useQuoteHeaderSave`) |
| `lib/` | Filter builders, row mappers, constants (`quotesFilters.ts`, `buildQuoteOfferRows.ts`) |

## When refactoring

- Match conventions in the target feature; use `quotes` as the template for new structure.
- Legacy flat files (e.g. `components/InvoiceHeaderForm.tsx`) may remain until touched—then migrate to grouped folders.
